body:
It would be good to be able to have a very simple widget that allows you to clear all the refinements and current query.

It's like a "start over" button in case of emergency/lost user.
# API

``` js
search.addWidget(
  instantsearch.widgets.hitsPerPageSelector({
    container: '#clear-all-selector',
    // cssClasses: {root, header, body, link, footer}
    // templates: {header, body, footer}
    // label: clear all
    // hideContainerWhenNoRefinements: true
  })
);
```

Default rendering output:

``` html
<div class="ais-clear-all">
  <div class="ais-clear-all--header ais-header">[custom header template]</div>
  <div class="ais-clear-all--body">
      <a class="ais-clear-all--link" href={url}>clear all</a>
  </div>
  <div class="ais-clear-all--footer ais-footer">[custom footer template]</div>
</div>
```

Data passed to the item template:
- url, in case you want to have a link instead of a button
- label

Put the onClick on the item template, like it's done for toggle

comments.body:
Here is the API I'm going for (using #378) :

``` js
instantsearch.widgets.clearAllRefinedValues({
  container: '#clear-all-link',
  cssClasses: {root, header, item, link, footer},
  templates: {
    header: '',
    item: '<a class="{{ cssClasses.link }}" href="{{url}}">Clear all</a>', // Called with {cssClasses, url}
    footer: ''
  },
  hideContainerWhenNoRefinements: true
})
```

I didn't include the `label` parameter from the main API proposal because we don't have such a thing in the stats widget which is also using constant text.
